Description: scene: Tell programs when their surfaces may show depth inside them
 .
 StereoDepthStates sends every followed surface its desktop depth state from
 StereoDepth's own rules whenever it may have changed: a window activated,
 raised, moved, pinned, minimized or put on another output, an output switched
 into or out of a 3D mode, a surface newly followed.
 .
 - StereoDepth::isAwake(): the window is shown on a stereo output and is the
   active window on top of what it overlaps, what pops up, a panel, the
   desktop, a window pinned above the others, or an active fullscreen window;
   a window in the pile behind the active one, or pinned below, lies flat.
 - StereoDepth::outputEdges(): the edges of the window's frame on its output's
   edge.
 - A popup's declared place is its level, under the rules popups already
   follow: at the output's edge it stays at the screen, and it is never behind
   the popup it was opened from. It takes no share of the popped limit. A
   window that is not a popup keeps its place in the stack.
 - A pair marked as the desktop's own depth is still drawn per eye, but
   Window::holdsStereoContent() leaves it out: it is not 3D content for the
   automatic 3D mode switch, stereo screenshots or the depth estimator.
 .
 testStereoDepthExchange covers each of these from a client.
